Content

The MIT license above covers the code. It does not cover the guide's content,
which is Copyright (c) 2026 Yūnus Andréasson, all rights reserved:

- the written guide in all five languages: the place guides and timeline in
  src/content/, and the page copy in src/i18n/ui.ts and in the copy blocks of
  src/components/views/
- the photographs by Yūnus Andréasson (@andreasson.photo), credited on the site:
  src/assets/photos/own*.jpg
- the illustrated hero plates: src/assets/places/
- the name myGjakova and the clock-tower mark, public/favicon.svg, with
  everything drawn from it: the icons and logo.png in public/, and the share
  cards public/og-default.jpg and public/og/

Third-party material keeps its own license:

- The other 29 photographs and scans in src/assets/photos/ come from Wikimedia
  Commons. Each is under the license listed beside it in docs/IMAGES.md
  (public domain, CC0, CC BY 2.0, CC BY 4.0, CC BY-SA 3.0 or CC BY-SA 4.0), with
  its author and file page, and the site credits each one where it appears.
- public/map/gjakova.pmtiles holds map data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors,
  under the Open Database License, extracted from a Protomaps build.
- public/map/glyphs/ holds Noto Sans glyphs, under the SIL Open Font License
  1.1.
- public/map/style.json is generated from @protomaps/basemaps, under the BSD
  3-Clause License.
- scripts/data/kosovo.geojson is the Kosovo boundary from Natural Earth, in the
  public domain.
- .claude/skills/astro/ is the Astro team's agent skill, under the MIT License.
